      {
        "base": "https://www.n4l.co.nz/category/alerts/feed/",
        "language": null,
        "type": "text/html",
        "value": "<p><div class=\"et_pb_section et_pb_section_9 et_pb_with_background et_section_regular\">\n\t\t\t\t\n\t\t\t\t\n\t\t\t\t\n\t\t\t\t\n\t\t\t\t\n\t\t\t\t\n\t\t\t\t<div class=\"et_pb_row et_pb_row_9\">\n\t\t\t\t<div class=\"et_pb_column et_pb_column_4_4 et_pb_column_9  et_pb_css_mix_blend_mode_passthrough et-last-child\">\n\t\t\t\t\n\t\t\t\t\n\t\t\t\t\n\t\t\t\t\n\t\t\t\t<div class=\"et_pb_module et_pb_text et_pb_text_9  et_pb_text_align_left et_pb_bg_layout_light\">\n\t\t\t\t\n\t\t\t\t\n\t\t\t\t\n\t\t\t\t\n\t\t\t\t<div class=\"et_pb_text_inner\"><p>N4L has made a change to the GlobalProtect settings, which will affect users using the GlobalProtect VPN client to log in remotely.</p>\n<p>Previously, GlobalProtect was configured with an \u201calways on\u201d setting, which meant it automatically reconnected to the school firewall when a user logged into the laptop. However, we\u2019ve identified that \u201calways on\u201d has been causing issues when users are actually onsite at school using the school network.</p>\n<p><strong>To prevent these issues, N4L has turned off the \u201calways on\u201d setting.</strong></p>\n<p>This means users who want to use GlobalProtect VPN to securely login to the school network remotely will now need to manually connect by opening the GlobalProtect client and clicking \u201cConnect\u201d.</p>\n<p><strong>For Microsoft users:</strong></p>\n<p>In the bottom right corner of the status tray, click on the \u201cglobe\u201d icon and select \u201cConnect\u201d<br /><a href=\"https://www.n4l.co.nz/wp-content/uploads/2026/05/Windows-GP-Icon.png\"><img alt=\"\" class=\"wp-image-11801 alignnone size-medium\" height=\"173\" src=\"https://www.n4l.co.nz/wp-content/uploads/2026/05/Windows-GP-Icon-300x173.png\" width=\"300\" /></a></p>\n<p><b>For Apple Mac users:</b></p>\n<p><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">Click on the \u201cglobe\u201d icon in the top right corner, then select \u201cConnect\u201d<br /><a href=\"https://www.n4l.co.nz/wp-content/uploads/2026/05/MAC-GP-Icon.png\"><img alt=\"\" class=\"wp-image-11802 alignnone size-medium\" height=\"71\" src=\"https://www.n4l.co.nz/wp-content/uploads/2026/05/MAC-GP-Icon-300x71.png\" width=\"300\" /></a><br /></span></p>\n<p>If you have any questions, our friendly Customer Support team is here to help. Contact us on <strong>support@n4l.co.nz </strong>or<strong> 0800 532 764</strong>.</p></div>\n\t\t\t</div>\n\t\t\t</div>\n\t\t\t\t\n\t\t\t\t\n\t\t\t\t\n\t\t\t\t\n\t\t\t</div>\n\t\t\t\t\n\t\t\t\t\n\t\t\t</div></p>\n<p>The post <a href=\"https://www.n4l.co.nz/important-update-to-globalprotect-setting/\">IMPORTANT: Update to GlobalProtect setting</a> appeared first on <a href=\"https://www.n4l.co.nz\">Network for Learning | N4L</a>.</p>"
      }
